                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most geographical"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2019f24-1d21-3d15-9ea8-0879fb86de64",
                        "entry_id": "4fa3281b-8690-3077-880b-560fc49eefa2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to geography."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "498c9067-8415-47f8-9d19-70265ae6f150",
                                "sense_id": "f2019f24-1d21-3d15-9ea8-0879fb86de64",
                                "text": "Morality knows nothing of geographical boundaries, or distinctions of race."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81fc468e-b501-404a-8e4d-35201536b00e",
                                "sense_id": "f2019f24-1d21-3d15-9ea8-0879fb86de64",
                                "text": "ONE OF the facts which define the United States is that its national and its imperial boundaries are the same. Another is that it is a political unit which occupies a remarkably compact geographical unit of continental extent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbe17b72-abdd-433b-958c-0bdf1ef71ea1",
                                "sense_id": "f2019f24-1d21-3d15-9ea8-0879fb86de64",
                                "text": "Clearly, the plane of the frame must be dominant, since that is the only plane that actually exists on the screen. Composition for this plane, however, is often influenced by factors in the geographical plane since, unless we are dealing with animation, a photographer or cinematographer must compose for the frame plane in the geographical plane."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "a2ebc56a-b2fb-4978-b1e7-792244eeb8ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "4fa3281b-8690-3077-880b-560fc49eefa2",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "f2019f24-1d21-3d15-9ea8-0879fb86de64"
                        ],
